## Overview

### Purpose
Build a proof-of-concept autonomous agent that routes user queries to appropriate tools and agents using LLM-based decision-making.

### Key Design Philosophy
**ONE smart component (Agent Layer), everything else is dumb infrastructure.**

```
User -> External UI/Client -> API Adapter -> Agent Layer (SMART) -> Infrastructure (dumb)
                                         ↓
                              ┌──────────┼──────────┐
                              ↓          ↓          ↓
                          LLM Service  Storage  Orchestrator
                                                    ↓
                                              MCP/A2A Tools
```

### What Makes This Architecture Special
1. **Agent Layer has ALL intelligence** - Main script, orchestrator, connectors are pure infrastructure
2. **Reusable Agent Layer** - Same component builds main agent, MCP agents, A2A agents
3. **Clean separation** - LLM calls vs tool executions logged separately
4. **Dual mode support** - Streaming and non-streaming throughout the stack
5. **Protocol agnostic** - MCP and A2A treated uniformly through interfaces

